# Embabel Me appliance — copy to `.env` in this directory and edit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# docker compose reads this file automatically. Nothing here is baked into an
# image; every value is read at container start, so editing it and running
# `docker compose up -d` is enough to apply a change.

# ── Required: at least one model provider ───────────────────────────────────
# The assistant cannot answer without one. OpenAI is the default provider for
# the shipped model configuration; Anthropic is used by the app builder.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Timezone ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The containers run UTC unless told otherwise, which makes the assistant's
# clock hours off for most of the planet. setup.py detects your host's zone and
# writes this for you; set it yourself only to override (IANA name).
#TZ=Australia/Sydney

# ── MCP access ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# You normally do NOT set these: first-run setup (./setup.py) mints an MCP
# bearer token bound to the account you create, and offers to wire Claude Code
# on the spot. Set them here only for scripted deployments that skip the
# wizard (openssl rand -hex 32). A setup-minted token takes precedence.
#EMBABEL_MCP_API_TOKEN=
#EMBABEL_MCP_API_TOKEN_USER=

# ── Authorization fallback ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without an external organization role provider, both appliance modes grant
# every authenticated principal the admin role by default. Set this to `user`
# to opt out; that removes admin access from every authenticated principal.
#ORG_ROLE_FALLBACK=user

# ── Optional: integration credentials ───────────────────────────────────────
# Each unlocks a capability and is inert when empty. Credentials are resolved at
# the integration layer and never injected into a prompt — the assistant can call
# a tool that needs a token without the model ever seeing it.
#BRAVE_API_KEY=            # web search
#GITHUB_TOKEN=             # GitHub realm: issues, PRs, repositories — and cloning PRIVATE
                          # realms/world templates. Usually needs no entry here: setup.py
                          # takes GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN
                          # from your shell, or the gh CLI's token, for that run.
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=       # chat with the assistant from Telegram
#SLACK_APP_TOKEN=          # chat with the assistant from Slack

# ── Version ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The appliance tag. Every Embabel image in the compose file moves together;
# pin this to a release rather than tracking a floating tag.
#EMBABEL_VERSION=0.2.0-SNAPSHOT

# ── World template ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The git repo NEW worlds are cloned from — how a preconfigured appliance ships
# (an industry world with its realms preinstalled, for example). Normally set
# for you by `./me.py --world <repo>`; applies when a world is FIRST created,
# and never reshapes an existing one.
#ASSISTANT_BOOTSTRAP_WORLD=https://github.com/embabel/default-world.git

# ── Optional services ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Turn profile-gated services on here rather than passing `--profile` ad hoc:
# compose reconciles to the ACTIVE profile set on every `up`, so an ad-hoc
# profile means the next plain `up` silently stops those containers. It is ONE
# comma-separated list — set every profile you want on the same line.
#
#   openwebui — Open WebUI as an alternative chat front-end on :4245
#
# The Grafana dashboards are NOT here: they are ordinary services and run by
# default. A profile can only ever be OFF by default (compose activates one
# solely when COMPOSE_PROFILES names it), and this appliance is meant to start
# with no .env at all — so a profile would have meant no dashboards for anyone
# who never created this file. Turn them off by deleting the two services from
# docker-compose.yml.
#COMPOSE_PROFILES=openwebui
#OPEN_WEBUI_SECRET_KEY=
#OPEN_WEBUI_DEFAULT_MODEL=gpt-4.1
# How long Prometheus keeps samples. Costs disk in the prometheus volume.
#PROMETHEUS_RETENTION=15d

# ── Ports (host side) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All bind to 127.0.0.1 — see the security note in README.md before changing.
#ASSISTANT_PORT=4242
#NEO4J_BROWSER_PORT=4243
#NEO4J_BOLT_PORT=4244
#OPEN_WEBUI_PORT=4245
#GRAFANA_PORT=4246
#PROMETHEUS_PORT=4247

# ── The Worlds console ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The console (4343) asks you to sign in with your appliance account. To skip
# that on a single-user machine, put the same credentials here and its proxy
# authenticates for you. ANYONE who can reach 4343 is then this user — fine on a
# laptop bound to 127.0.0.1, wrong on a shared server.
#WORLDS_CONSOLE_USER=
#WORLDS_CONSOLE_PASSWORD=

# ── The Worlds mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same image, same data, different front: the world runtime on the 43xx block.
#   docker compose -f docker-compose-worlds.yml up -d
# Run ONE mode at a time — see "Two modes" in README.md.
#WORLDS_PORT=4342
# Externally visible origin for the Worlds mode, if proxied — no trailing slash.
#WORLDS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4342

# ── Tuning ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Embedding model. The default is LOCAL — Qwen3-Embedding 0.6B, served by
# Docker Model Runner on the host (see the `models:` element in
# docker-compose.yml), so memory and document search cost no API tokens. Set a
# provider model such as text-embedding-3-small (needs OPENAI_API_KEY) to opt
# out of local embeddings. A LOCAL value must be the registry-qualified id the
# runner reports (curl -s localhost:12434/engines/v1/models), not the pull
# name. CHANGING THIS ON AN EXISTING INSTALL is a migration, not a tweak:
# stored vectors were made by the old model, so run the re-embed from
# Settings → Embedding model after switching.
#ASSISTANT_EMBEDDING_MODEL=docker.io/ai/qwen3-embedding:0.6B-F16
# `none` = raw Tika text extraction; makes the (multi-GB) docling image
# unnecessary at the cost of table/figure fidelity in PDFs and office docs.
#ASSISTANT_DOC_CONVERTER=docling
# Docling version, mirrored into GHCR from upstream quay.io (MIT). Pinned so a
# first run cannot be broken by an upstream retag.
#DOCLING_VERSION=v1.29.0
#NEO4J_PASSWORD=embabel-assistant
#NEO4J_HEAP=2G
#JAVA_OPTS=-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75

# ── Usage reporting ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The appliance reports anonymous usage data (counts and versions, never your
# data or code) to Embabel every 24 hours. Every field is listed in PHONE_HOME.md,
# and /api/v1/phone-home on your instance shows the exact JSON last sent.
#
# There is no setting here, deliberately: the collector is fixed in the image. A
# variable you could blank would be an opt-out by another name, and we would
# rather be straight about not offering one. Block it at your network if you must.

# ── Behind a proxy / on another host ────────────────────────────────────────
# The externally visible origin. OAuth callbacks, MCP resource indicators, and
# app/artifact links all compose from it. No trailing slash.
#ASSISTANT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4242

# ── Working on a realm ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PARENT directory of realm checkouts on this machine, bind-mounted
# read-only at /realms. A world can then load one in place, with no push and no
# clone by the server:
#
#   # config/realms.yml, in the world
#   - name: esg
#     path: /realms/realm-esg
#
# The parent rather than one realm, so adding a realm is a `git clone` rather
# than an edit here and a restart. `./worlds.py` offers to set this on first
# run and checks the path before writing it. The default is the realms/
# directory in this checkout.
#
# macOS: the path must be inside Docker Desktop's file sharing list (Settings →
# Resources → File sharing), or the mount is silently EMPTY. /Users is shared by
# default, so a path under your home directory needs nothing.
#EMBABEL_REALMS_DIR=/Users/you/dev/realms

# ── Which door ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The mode this appliance was last started as: `me` (the personal assistant) or
# `worlds` (the world runtime and its console). setup.py writes it the first time
# a mode starts, and `embabel up` with no --me/--worlds returns to it.
#
# It exists because the two defaults disagreed by design — the installer opens
# the Me door, the `embabel` command opens Worlds — so without a record, stopping
# and starting again could hand you the other product on the same graph.
#EMBABEL_MODE=me
